  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Prerelease. beta.2 continues paused turns automatically: a Claude turn whose server-side tool loop pauses is carried on for you, with the blocks and token usage of every round folded into one response, so OuroStopReason.Paused now only surfaces when a turn paused more times than the budget allows. beta.2 adds provider failover: set ChatOptions.FallbackModels or OuroClient.SetDefaultFallback and a call that a provider cannot serve is retried on the next model in the chain, transient failures only. OnChatCompleted now fires once per attempt (ChatCompletedArgs gains Attempt and NextModel), so a failed attempt is still logged. beta.2 adds Anthropic as a second provider: Claude models route through the same client via the OuroborosOptions overload of AddOuroboros. Structured output (ChatOptions.ResponseType) works on both providers from one schema, and JsonSchemaGenerator is public so you can check a type or inspect what is actually sent. Requests on either provider can opt into server-side code execution (OuroServerTools.CodeExecution) - results arrive as OuroCodeExecutionBlock entries with stdout, exit code and generated-file references - and file I/O via UploadFileAsync / DownloadFileAsync / DeleteFileAsync plus ChatOptions.Attachments. The OpenAI path moved off Betalgo onto the official OpenAI SDK over the Responses API; ChatOptions.User is now ChatOptions.OpenAi.User, and StopSequences are refused on OpenAI because the Responses API has no stop parameter. Responses now carry typed content blocks and an OuroStopReason (truncation and paused tool loops are finally visible). Adds per-attempt timeouts (ChatOptions.Timeout), CancellationToken support, and a retry policy that no longer retries timeouts. A throwing OnChatCompleted hook no longer fails the chat it was logging - see OnChatCompletedFailure. ChatAsync no longer mutates the caller's ChatOptions. The TypeMerger dependency is gone: the template engine builds its own render context now, which also means a global context passed as an ExpandoObject reaches the template instead of being silently dropped. 5.0.0 is a breaking release that removes the provider SDK from the public API; see MIGRATION_4.4_to_5.0.md.",
